{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363451-introduced-facts-your-favorite-examples","id":1363451,"title":"Introduced Facts: Your Favorite Examples","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-26T08:16:09-08:00","id":1363451,"title":"Introduced Facts: Your Favorite Examples","content":"How have the PCs in your games made use of the Introducing a Fact mechanics in 3e? Any notable examples from your games you'd like to mention?<br /> <br /> My players are eager to see what other people have gotten away with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T08:43:40-08:00","id":1363452,"title":"","content":"I've got one from just last night!<br /> <br /> My players were trying to navigate between two big cities in the Underworld, across an ever-shifting field of rusted weapons. They knew there was trade between the two, and the Twilight decided to introduce a fact that there were enchanted signposts between the two, always pointing in the right direction. Ten-odd successes later, it was cannon that there was a network of severed arms dangling from poles, ready to direct you to the next stop on the trade route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T14:08:20-08:00","id":1363511,"title":"","content":"My Twilight Chef was part of a group trying to kill a Satrap, and we needed to find a way to make it discrete. We decided that the best method would be poisoning his food, in a way that nobody would question too deeply, as he himself wasn't necessarily well-liked even by his family. Give them a good enough excuse and the Magistrates wouldn't look deeper.<br /> <br /> Did you know that <i>fugu</i> is a delicacy amongst the Dynasts? I mean, after six successes on my Twilight's Lore (Regional Delicacies) roll, it was.<br /> <br /> Said Chef took Limit because preparing <i>fugu</i> properly enough to fool most senses but is still poisoned and knowingly serving it went against her Pride as a chef.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T17:25:16-08:00","id":1363538,"title":"","content":"I think my personal favorite still is when on a whim Robin the Eclipse decided that a ooc chat rumor of the night character was made cannon a joke that the night caste assassin where if you said their name/title three times in front of a mirror they would appear. It's funnily enough the most remembered fact my characters made and is referenced multiple times. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14713-chronos12","name":"Chronos12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14713_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T15:04:21-08:00","id":1363687,"title":"","content":"&quot;All the buildings built like [the building we're currently trapped in by massive army] actually have secret tunnels. And because the tunnels are absolutely top secret, most children know about them. That makes sense right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T04:11:22-08:00","id":1363940,"title":"","content":"&quot;There are rumours in this part of the Hundred Kingdoms about a great city, lost in the time between Contagion and the coming of the Fae, where a great arch that leads to heaven, hell and the realm of dead existed before that place's fall to the hosts of chaos.&quot; - from a player getting dramatic in his desire for a way to escape the Wyld Hunt... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And so Sirap, the mysterious City of Four Portals, hidden from the eyes of heaven for gods, demons, dead and fae to bargain, intrigue and mingle freely, among themselves and with mortals bold, cunning or foolhardy enough to dare so, under the careful ministrations of the Body of Eight Powers - and soon to be base of a whole campaign - was born.<br /> <br /> (I'll also admit, a little loosely inspired in part by Hellsalem's Lot from Blood Blockade Battlefront)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-29-2020, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T02:48:39-08:00","id":1368017,"title":"","content":"I took our party to the plateau of Leng, to try and find and destroy the High Priest Not To Be Described (aka the Elder Hierophant, aka the Tcho-Tcho Lama of Leng). Anyway, to save time we travelled through the Forbidden Forest of Worms, where... well, a lot of bad things happened. (I did warn them it was an evil forest! I gave them the option of going round it!)<br /> <br /> Anyway, after travelling to the Black Monastery of Leng (well, its site, as it had mysteriously vanished leaving only a basement level where we found a stolen mummy of the First Pharoah), and then back through the forest, we discovered that (our Twilight) Cid Highwind's airship had been eaten by giant worms, including his crew, leaving only the indigestible First Age engine.<br /> <br /> Which kind of made it difficult to get home.<br /> <br /> Luckily, my Zenith, Brother Alazar, comes from the plateau of Leng, so knew the area. So I declared that there were a number of foul and decadent sorcerers who make it their home, and one lives a few days travel away. It was Difficulty 3: I think the ST felt it fit, and that as I said they were evil and decadent sorcerers, as opposed to really friendly and helpful ones, it seemed reasonable.<br /> <br /> So, we travelled to the Black Tower of an evil sorcerer, and tricked him into lending us a demon-pulled chariot, which we used to travel back home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T04:49:59-08:00","id":1368893,"title":"","content":"I can't go into details too much because it's a bit long, but the most important infos are these ones :<br /> <br /> There was first a campaign of 2 years where the players were from an Egyptian-like people, that stopped an invasion from Aztec-like people (among other things happening in the campaign).<br /> <br /> Next year I run a Campaign from the remnants of the Aztec-like people, totally devastated because they are on the verge of extinction after the war<br /> <br /> In this new campaign, they investigate one of their tribe that has been attacked by feys, who took the body of PC Eclipse relative, and they wonder why ?<br /> <br /> One character states a fact &quot;That's because the City X the feys are in war with is protected against the Wild, and they need the blood of someone related to the God-King that created the city (former Twilight player in the campaign of 2 years) to infiltrate it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It works. Me and the other player that played the last campaign looked into each other eyes trying to recall the lore of the last campaign (the other players were not from the last campaign)<br /> <br /> Suddenly we realize : &quot;Yeah, and this means that PC Eclipse is actually a descendant of the God-King and legitimate heir to the throne of City X&quot;, City X also being at war with the players tribes<br /> <br /> PC Eclipse who had a Defining Intimacy of hating City X : &quot;NOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T05:09:03-08:00","id":1368895,"title":"","content":"My players are very fond of introducing facts to either bypass part of the problem, create a new one or extend a gag.<br /> <br /> At some point someone introduced a fact that cows and goats do not get along well at all, each harboring a deep ingrained resentment towards the other. It complicates how you raise those herds. Goats have to be fed first, but cows have to be fed more, to give both of them an illusion of one upping the other and stuff.<br /> <br /> One time the corsairs were stopped in a realm blockade in the inland sea, and the Night contested the officer's legal babble to state an opening he could legally use. Some tension ensued.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T06:49:29-08:00","id":1368917,"title":"","content":"So in the first session, the Full Moon Olaf Keelbreaker revealed to the other players his tragic backstory; a huge armoured Dragonblood came to his fishing village with soldiers, and burnt it to the ground. Olaf exalted as a Lunar, but the inexperienced young Casteless was defeated and fell into the sea. Ever since then, he's tried to seek out the Dragonblood who destroyed his village, and all he has is a bit of heraldry he ripped off a soldier's armour.<br /> <br /> He gave it to the No Moon, who did some research, rolled to Establish a Fact, and declared that it was a mercenary band called the World Eaters. Hehehe....<br /> <br /> If you know Warhammer 40k canon, you may know that the World Eaters were a Space Marine legion who wore white-and-blue. Later, they all became Khorne Berzerkers, and switched to red uniforms.<br /> <br /> So, when the PCs encountered the World Eaters, a group of ashigaru mercenaries led by Dragonblooded samurai and yamabushi, they sometimes wore red, and sometimes wore white-and-blue. Why? Well, because they're the World Eaters right?<br /> <br /> But what Realm House is Japanese-themed, has yamabushi, wears white-and-blue? And ended up with only one legion, a legion that famously uses red (grubby) uniforms?<br /> <br /> Yeah, House Tepet. Who I intended to be secretly the main antagonists of the game <i>all along</i>.<br /> <br /> If the player hadn't declared that they were the World Eaters, maybe players would have gone &quot;hmm, why do these Dragonblood wear white-and-blue or red?&quot; much earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T08:53:13-08:00","id":1368943,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, House Ragara is aligned with Nurgle afterall and amusingly close to the original Death Guard colours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T09:54:30-08:00","id":1368959,"title":"","content":"&gt;Cynis Ganan wears purple (for Mnemon) and gold trim (for Cynis).<br /> &gt;Cynis<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://nightsatthegametable.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/Emperors-Children-2.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Aww crap...</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-19-2020, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T23:49:23-08:00","id":1369100,"title":"","content":"My Lunar character has a majestic bird of prey as their Spirit Shape (a golden hawk, iirc).<br /> <br /> My Zenith chef/medic knows very little bird biology, but has an excellent Lore score with a domain concerning the uses of plants.<br /> <br /> The Zenith established a fact about bird seed being the best diet to eat when recovering from wounds, so the very carnivorous (and lightly wounded) Lunar has on several occasions refused/thrown in the Zenith's face offerings of seeds and, I quote, &quot;stared daggers&quot; at him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}